# TypeScript path aliases (Frontend)

Prefer configured path aliases over `../` climbs. Same-folder `./` is fine.

| Alias | Maps to | Use for |
|-------|---------|---------|
| `@/*` | `App/*` | App modules (`@/views/...`, `@/session`, `@/hooks`, …) |
| `api` / `api/*` | federated remote types | GraphQL hooks/types from `api/provider` |
| `design/*` | federated remote types | Components, styles, icons, router and widgets from the design system |
| `^/*` | repo root | Rare cross-package paths outside App |

```ts
// ❌
import { labelFor } from '../tree';
import { Experiments } from '../../../experiments';

// ✅
import { labelFor } from '@/views/experiments/tree-of-life/tree';
import { Experiments } from '@/views/experiments';
import { Button } from 'design/components';
import { Kicl_TaxonVisualDocument, useQuery } from 'api/provider';
```

When editing imports, rewrite reachable relatives to the matching alias in the same change.

**Exception:** Vite/bootstrap config under `App/.client` and `App/.server` may keep relatives for JSON/config loaded before aliases exist (e.g. `get-alias.ts` → `../../tsconfig.json`).
